  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 240 PM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nSaturday-Early Next Week:\nIncreasing mid-level heights into this weekend as a longwave\ntrough axis shifts east of the region. This will allow\ntemperatures to warm into the 90s, with some locations even\npushing near 100 in far southeast KS and southwest MO. Dewpoints\ninto the upper 60s and lower 70s, will support daily heat index\nvalues around 100 to 105 degrees. LREF continues to suggest low\nprobabilities of exceeding 105 in our area, with chances \nlimited to around < 10%. Nonetheless, it is plausible headlines \nmay need introduced as a result of the multi-day aspect of the \nheat. As we progress through the weekend into early next week, \nthe NWS HeatRisk depicts widespread Major (3 of 4) for potential\nheat- related impacts.\n\nRain chances appear to be low through this period, though not\nzero as we remain on the eastern periphery of the ridge. Any\nsubtle breakdowns in the ridge may allow shortwave energy to\ntranslate through the area. By mid-next week, ensembles are\nbeginning to hint at the return of an active pattern as the\nridge becomes displaced back west.",
